# Changes
## Market:
- Selling starts with a list of everything you carry, each item with its picture and a **[ Sell ]** button; then you set how many and the price for just that item
- You can change the price of your listings (and how many are bought at a time) and add more of the same item to a listing whenever you like. Adding more runs the listing for its full time again
- Browsing shows every listing in one scrolling list instead of pages of 10, so pricier listings are no longer easy to miss
- New **Market** page on the website: everything players and the server sell right now, searchable
- **My SMP Profile** now shows your **Market Inbox** (earnings and items waiting for you in `/market`) and your **Pets**
- Shulker boxes, chests, banners and decorated pots now have pictures on the info page and the website
- Ask Merl what to sell something for: *"how much should I sell diamonds for?"*, *"what's this worth?"* (the item in your hand). She looks at what it sold for lately and what it's listed for now

## Gameplay:
- Mini blocks of the new cinnabar, sulfur and poplar blocks: in the stonecutter, and sometimes from Wandering Traders
- Crops grow faster while it rains on them
- Better Mending: sneak and right-click an anvil to repair the Mending item in your hand with your experience
- AFK players no longer count when it's about skipping the night: the players who are actually there decide
- Tree chopping no longer takes the tree next to it along when their branches or leaves touch
- Graves, Waypoint Hubs and the clickable spots at spawn work inside every claim, also when you aren't a member of it

## Pets:
- Pets no longer fly through you during their moves
- While you're AFK your pet roams around you on its own, and goes back to its move when you're back
- Pet particles no longer drift into your view

## World Map:
- Waypoint Hub pins have the colour of the hub's name in game, and the hub's own icon in their popup
- The names of who's online in the status card jump to that player on the map

## Website:
- Waypoint Hubs on My SMP Profile show the hub's own icon instead of your head
- The advancements Nice Things adds to the vanilla tabs now show up in those tabs on the Statistics page and My SMP Profile

# Fixes
- Tenkū's explosion attack, the Rusta's Random Totem anvils, the Stonepiercer and Heavy Shot scrolls, the spawn decorations and the villager job site highlight used a block format 26.3 no longer reads
- The Congress Assembled advancement was granted for using any trial key on any vault; now only a Trial Key of Roots counts
- The Supercharged advancement's description: it's about having Haste II, wherever it comes from
